<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas Bowdich</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">visited Kumasi 1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas Bowdich was an English traveller and writer who visited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumasi">Kumasi</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> capital, as a British envoy in 1817. His published account is a major early European source on the Ashanti Empire. He described wide paved roads, buildings decorated with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adinkra">Adinkra symbols</a>, a disciplined standing army and elaborate court ceremonies.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thomas-bowdich.jpg" alt="Thomas Bowdich" width="320" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: William Derby · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thomas_Edward_Bowdich.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
